00:30:57.650 --> 00:30:59.240
Premium versus standard tier.

00:30:59.240 --> 00:31:01.070
This has to do with
Google's backbone.

00:31:01.070 --> 00:31:01.620
Right?

00:31:01.620 --> 00:31:03.245
So I told you I'd
mention this earlier.

00:31:03.245 --> 00:31:04.453
I told you I'd talk about it.

00:31:04.453 --> 00:31:07.010
So really what this is is
Google has a philosophy of we

00:31:07.010 --> 00:31:09.067
want to control your
traffic as much as possible

00:31:09.067 --> 00:31:10.400
in terms of the user experience.

00:31:10.400 --> 00:31:11.120
Right?

00:31:11.120 --> 00:31:14.120
So if you select premium
network, what that means is

00:31:14.120 --> 00:31:16.550
if you have something
in, say, the east coast,

00:31:16.550 --> 00:31:18.050
but the user's on
the west coast,

00:31:18.050 --> 00:31:19.280
we're going to use
Google's backbone

00:31:19.280 --> 00:31:21.290
to deliver that traffic all
the way to the west coast.

00:31:21.290 --> 00:31:21.500
Right?

00:31:21.500 --> 00:31:23.010
Because when it's
on our backbone,

00:31:23.010 --> 00:31:24.090
we control that quality.

00:31:24.090 --> 00:31:24.590
Right?

00:31:24.590 --> 00:31:26.630
We can make sure that
that packet is not

00:31:26.630 --> 00:31:28.160
getting bogged down
in the internet

00:31:28.160 --> 00:31:29.720
or being congested by things.

00:31:29.720 --> 00:31:31.880
So that's what premium tier is.

00:31:31.880 --> 00:31:34.800
Now, standard tier was designed
to help cost manage this stuff.

00:31:34.800 --> 00:31:35.300
Right?

00:31:35.300 --> 00:31:36.717
So what happens
in standard tier--

00:31:36.717 --> 00:31:39.950
let's take our east
coast origination device.

00:31:39.950 --> 00:31:42.200
It would say, dump it off
to an ISP in the east coast.

00:31:42.200 --> 00:31:43.640
That ISP would
pick up that packet

00:31:43.640 --> 00:31:45.110
and take it all the
way to the west coast.

00:31:45.110 --> 00:31:46.650
But again, you're not
using Google's backbone.

00:31:46.650 --> 00:31:48.260
You're just using the
internet at large.

00:31:48.260 --> 00:31:49.177
STEPHANIE WONG: Right.

00:31:49.177 --> 00:31:49.910
OK.

00:31:49.910 --> 00:31:51.250
RYAN PRZYBYL: So that's
the difference here.

